# Results: nested subject-wise CV

Outer 4-fold × inner 3-fold CV, split by subject. 1-s windows, 75% overlap (1,197 per subject). Hyper-parameter grid: lr {0.001, 0.0001} × dropout {0.25, 0.5}. Every subject is tested exactly once; metrics are computed once on the pooled outer-test predictions. Subject probability = mean of its segment probabilities, threshold 0.5. Positive class = more severe group.

**Incomplete (not shown):** c1_none_vs_dep / EEGNet: 1/4 outer folds; c1_none_vs_dep / ShallowFBCSPNet: 1/4 outer folds; c1_none_vs_dep / Deep4Net: 1/4 outer folds; c2_nonemild_vs_severe / EEGNet: 1/4 outer folds; c2_nonemild_vs_severe / ShallowFBCSPNet: 1/4 outer folds; c2_nonemild_vs_severe / Deep4Net: 1/4 outer folds; c3_mild_vs_severe / EEGNet: 3/4 outer folds; c3_mild_vs_severe / Deep4Net: 2/4 outer folds

